Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: Don't fallback to shared VM for VM_BIND

If the user wants a userspace managed VM (EN_VM_BIND) don't silently
fall back to shared VM.

BACKPORT of mainline commit 3b35a5c528ba ("drm/msm: Don't fallback to shared VM for VM_BIND").
Part of Rob Clark's 2026-07-29 drm/msm context/VM hardening series
(Message-ID 20260729155609.20190-*, patches 2..18), merged for 7.3.
None of it is in 7.2.x, which is what kernel/SOURCE.pin points at.

The fix we are actually after. msm_gpu_create_private_vm() silently handed
back the global kernel-managed VM when per-process pgtable creation failed,
even for a userspace-managed (EN_VM_BIND) client. Turnip then does its own
address management against a VM it does not own, and the GPU takes a storm
of `type=TRANSLATION source=UCHE` faults -- mesa#14656, reported on A740,
which is every qcs8550-* board we ship. With the fix the ioctl fails
honestly, tu_try_enable_vm_bind() returns non-zero and Turnip drops to the
legacy submit path instead.

---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_drv.c
@@ -244,7 +244,8 @@ struct drm_gpuvm *msm_context_vm(struct drm_device *dev, struct msm_context *ctx
 	if (!ctx->vm) {
 		vm = msm_gpu_create_private_vm(
 			priv->gpu, current, !ctx->userspace_managed_vm);
-		smp_store_release(&ctx->vm, vm);
+		if (!IS_ERR_OR_NULL(vm))
+			smp_store_release(&ctx->vm, vm);
 	}
 
 	return ctx->vm;
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gpu.c
@@ -875,7 +875,7 @@ msm_gpu_create_private_vm(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct task_struct *task,
 			to_msm_vm(vm)->pid = get_pid(task_pid(task));
 	}
 
-	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(vm))
+	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(vm) && kernel_managed)
 		vm = drm_gpuvm_get(gpu->vm);
 
 	return vm;
